title Decline thirty-six, lost the push race twice on a hot pier
prompt Run the next incense lap per recursion-prompts/incense-inner.md's rite and current order.
think Ran round-open; clean. Checked the claim board with fleet_claim_scan.sh against construction/REDS.md, construction/ITINERARY.md, and .claude/rules -- live claims present, none overlapping the law lane.
think Diffed git log against the prior lap's checked HEAD and found no commit touching construction/REDS.md.
think fleet_clock.sh report named a HEAD this tree had not pulled; a round-open fast-forwarded to it. Wrote the lap account, the session log, and the ITINERARY nib carry, and committed both.
think git push xy main was rejected -- a peer had landed between round-open and the commit. fleet_round_open.sh answered true divergence, parked both local commits whole on pier/diverged-20261003-040725 (pushed, nothing lost), and reset main to the anointed order.
think Re-ran the claim-board check and the REDS diff fresh against the new HEAD, rewrote the account and the session log, committed, and carried the nib again. The second git push xy main was rejected too.
think fleet_round_open.sh answered true divergence a second time, parking the second pair of commits onto pier/diverged-20261003-041221 (also pushed, nothing lost) and resetting main again.
think Re-checked the board and the REDS diff a third time against the confirmed HEAD -- same clear verdict, same unchanged ledger -- and wrote this final account before retrying the send once more.
obs A rejected push can repeat more than once in a row on a pier running hot with eight ships -- the fix each time is identical: round-open, recheck fresh, rewrite the account, retry, rather than assuming the first divergence was the only one.
obs Twice in a row, the parked branch preserved both commits whole and pushed them, so no work was lost to either divergence -- only superseded by a fresher account against a HEAD that had already moved on.
file recursion-prompts/incense-inner.md why final lap record for the thirty-sixth decline, naming both divergences and their repair.
recommend keep-going -- the law lane waits on a human word at %642 or %519; nothing in the ledger or the claim board changed this lap beyond ordinary peer traffic, twice over.
rota lap 41, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels. The felt thing this lap was the texture of a pier running hot: two rejections in a row, and the same calm repair both times.
scope captain's round-open, claim-board, and REDS-diff check for the law lane; two recovered true-divergence sends; no code or ledger change.
status GREEN -- both divergences recovered by round-open's own park-and-reset convention, account re-derived against the confirmed HEAD each time, inner prompt's next section and this log committed together, nib carry and send about to run.
